# Pass "avec-ads2": A Dog Said... Animal Prosthetics 2 beside this mod.
#
# SamBucher.ADogSaidAnimalProsthetics2, Workshop 3238353862, by SamBucher, which supports 1.4, 1.5 and 1.6. It
# declares no hard dependency, so this one line is the whole set. This mod says loadBefore for it, and 08 asserts
# that order before it asserts anything else: ADS 2 copies its category lists once, so a patch that loads after it
# lands in a list nobody reads.
#
# It is in the WSL cache since 2026-09-24, version 1.3.7, the same as the source this mod was written against. It was
# fetched with scripts/download-workshop-wsl.sh through the machine lock, at the owner's request, and it is not in
# the Windows Workshop: the staging script finds it as its second place, ~/workshop-cache.
# ORDER. The staging activates the mods a map names in the order of the map, and only then the mod under test, so
# ADS 2 alone would load BEFORE this mod: the first run of this pass (2026-09-24) read exactly that, and 08 failed on
# its first line, "should load before", with ADS 2 ahead of Dust Bunnies Renew. Naming this mod's own packageId with
# path: activates it at this position instead ("overlay replaces" in the staging output), which is the order the
# game's own sort gives from About.xml's loadBefore. Written by hand above the ADS 2 line, so it has to stay above.
#
# What this does and does not prove. The pass proves the order, once it is given, does what the mod needs. That
# About.xml asks for that order is proved offline, by Check-Claims. That the game's sort would produce it from
# that declaration is not proved by any run here: it would need the sort itself.
nelim.dustbunniesrenew   path:DustBunniesRenew/Mod
SamBucher.ADogSaidAnimalProsthetics2   3238353862
